{
  "name": "Simple Steps to Better Closet Storage",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Want to get your closet storage sorted so it actually works for you? It's easier than you think to make some big improvements! First off, measure your personal reachable zones. This is super important because it helps you figure out the ideal height for rods and shelves, making sure frequently used items are always within easy grasp, whether you're standing or seated. Next, consider going for shallower shelves. Trust me, it prevents things from getting lost in the back and makes everything more visible. Thinking about pull-out units or full-extension drawers? They're game-changers for accessing items without having to dig around. And don't forget about adjustability! Shelves that can be moved up or down as your needs change are incredibly valuable. The timing for these changes is flexible, but it’s best to consider them alongside any other closet renovations since shelf depth and door types can really impact your usable space. If you're looking to integrate these ideas with custom framing or nonstandard dimensions, HH Remodeling LLC can provide the professional help needed to make sure your new storage is perfectly tailored to you.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
